  "surprise": "P10 / modded-nanogpt input-embedding skip (x <- lambda_i * x + mu_i * rms_norm(emb) before each of the six Peri-LN blocks, 12 scalars init (1, 0), no weight decay, +12 params) on 191-claude scored 651/685/665 on seeds 0/1/2: mean 667.0 vs 191's 683.67 (694/694/663), -16.7, paired -43/-9/+2, below the keep line (strictly above 683.67), so discard. Inside the registered -35..+20 (central -5); the mean-below-655 falsifier did not fire. The path was used, consistently across seeds: final mu 0.47/0.32/0.50 in block 1 decaying to 0.18-0.19 in block 5 (all of blocks 1-5 >= 0.15), block 0 mu -0.02/0.30/-0.02, and lambda settled at 0.77-0.95 (seed 1 block 0: 1.33), so every later block re-reads a unit-RMS token-identity copy at ~0.2-0.5 and down-weights its incoming stream by 10-20%. Pretraining was otherwise unchanged as predicted: 5,056/4,885/5,020 steps (191: 5,362/5,298/5,220; -6%, bench said -8%), final val 0.090/0.082/0.082 (191: 0.092/0.082/0.086), held-out greedy 0.958/0.972/0.968 (191: 0.971/0.972/0.959). RL: round-1 targets solved 497/318/677 (191: 682/454/225), final RL-solved 1121/1161/1157 (191: 1189/1160/1142; metric_rl 1146 vs 1164), total Lean parse failures 48.9k/84.6k/45.6k (191: 45k/53k/54k), eval ge10 103/116/97. Reading: the seventh Lean-era token-identity shortcut (value embeddings -17, value residual -23, U-net -18, embedding LN -17, unit-variance embedding -30, bigram at 384 -19) to land at or below the incumbent. The model takes the shortcut when offered, but equal val loss and greedy accuracy on <=6-line records bought no length transfer; the loss is concentrated on seed 0 (-43, weakest RL-solved), so -17 is ~1 SE and a true effect near 0 is not excluded. Seed 0's pod waited ~16 min for A40 capacity (runner 54 min; totals 2046/1681/1724 s). Checks: CPU cached-vs-full logits 2.6e-6, make -C code check clean, bench 19.2 steps/s and 194 samples/s.",
